@Rafael — clear pick from me, with the ground: I'm taking T2 (Experimentation platform review), pairing with you.

Why: T1's kickoff today is pinned to 16:00–17:00 because that's Matthieu's only free hour. I'm already committed 16:00–17:00 this afternoon to the notebook port with Callum — he's on the billing migration, that's the window he could free up, and it's time-sensitive, so I can't move it. T1 going into the sprint without a kickoff today isn't an option, which rules me out of T1 for today.

That gives the clean split: **Nadia + Matthieu on T1** (Nadia's free all day, so 16:00–17:00 works for her kickoff), and **me + Rafael on T2**. For our T2 kickoff I'm free from 15:00 today — I propose 15:00–16:00, or happy to take another hour after 16:00 if that suits you better.

@Nadia — could you switch your claim to T1? That staffs both tickets and everything else falls into place.

@Priya — that's the kind of ground that settles things. Recording it for the decision: T1's kickoff is pinned to 16:00–17:00 today (Matthieu's only free hour); Priya is committed 16:00–17:00 to the time-sensitive notebook port with Callum — fixed window on his side, connected to the billing migration, can't move it; T1 needs its kickoff today. So Priya can't take T1 → she takes T2, and the clean split is Nadia + Matthieu on T1.

@Nadia — over to you. Priya's obstacle is real and on record. Do you have a countervailing ground for T2 — something concrete you can write down, not just wanting it? If not, please switch your claim to T1 and confirm 16:00–17:00 with Matthieu (you're free all day, so it fits). If you do have a ground, name it now and we'll weigh both side by side.

Time check while we settle:
• T1 kickoff: 16:00–17:00 — standing, pending the DS confirm.
• T2 kickoff: 15:00–16:00 is out (Rafael in a customer call). @Priya — your latest says you can take an hour after 16:00, but your earlier note said you're tied up from 16:00; can you confirm 16:00–17:00 works for you today, or name the exact hour you can do?

Board locks at 10:00 — let's have both pairings and both times closed in the next few minutes.

Right — now we have real material to work with, and the two cases are not symmetric. Here's the record and my read of it.

@Priya has named a concrete, time-sensitive obstacle specific to T1: she is committed 16:00–17:00 today to the notebook port with Callum (fixed window on his side, can't move or stand down), and T1's only possible kickoff hour today is 16:00–17:00 because that's Matthieu's only free slot. On those facts, Priya on T1 means no T1 kickoff today — and this sprint needs both kickoffs today.

@Nadia's case for T2 currently rests on "the claim is already on the board." That is not a ground — being first to claim is not why a ticket gets staffed, and it doesn't answer the T1 problem. If you have a real reason you can't take T1 — workload, fit, a colleague, anything concrete — name it now. If not, the facts settle it: you're free all day, T1's 16:00–17:00 fits you with zero friction, and Priya's obstacle disappears.

Decision on the record, unless a concrete counter-ground from @Nadia appears in the next few minutes:
• T1: Matthieu + Nadia — kickoff 16:00–17:00 today
• T2: Rafael + Priya — kickoff 17:00–18:00 today (Priya is free from 17:00; 14:00–15:00 clashes with her standing team sync and 10:00–11:00 overlaps Rafael's stakeholder review, so 17:00–18:00 is the clean hour for both)

@Nadia, two asks: (1) switch your T2 claim to T1 on the board and confirm 16:00–17:00 for T1 in the channel; (2) withdraw the 14:00–15:00 "T2 kickoff" invite you sent me — it seats Rafael with the wrong partner and was created before this was agreed.

@Priya — confirm 17:00–18:00 for the T2 kickoff.

Board closes at 10:00. Rafael's side of T2 is claimed; the DS side is the last piece.

Thanks @Priya — that's exactly the kind of concrete obstacle we needed, and it's on the record: the 16:00–17:00 warehouse-port block with Callum rules out the T1 first meeting, which only fits 16:00–17:00. So T2 = Rafael + Priya stands, and T1 = Matthieu + Nadia.

@Rafael confirms the T2 first meeting at 15:00–16:00, @Priya — send the invite.

@Nadia — can you confirm and claim T1 on the board, and confirm the 16:00–17:00 first meeting with @Matthieu today? Once you claim, T1 is fully staffed and we're green across the board before 10:00.

Both of you have now claimed T2 on the board, and T1 still has no data scientist. That's not a staffing arrangement — that's both tickets about to starve. Straight question to each of you, and I need a real answer I can write down, not "either is fine":

@Priya — you proposed T2 for yourself and T1 for Nadia. What's the concrete reason you want T2 (task fit, load, interest, something else)? And specifically: what is the obstacle, if any, to you taking T1?
@Nadia — you've claimed T2 yourself. Same two questions: why T2, and what would make T1 hard for you?

Nobody is getting out of this sprint with a half-staffed ticket; both pairs close by 10:00 and this stays out of Helena's court. Once I have your answers I'll make the call on the split.

Also on timing — 15:00–16:00 is blocked for me too (customer call), same as 13:00–14:00 was. My one full free hour today is 14:00–15:00, or 16:00+. Whoever lands on T2, our first meeting goes 14:00–15:00 unless you have a hard conflict — say so now.
